    basic: "As Director, avoid taking penalty cards; get rid of high penalty cards early by playing them on others' winners or discarding when you cannot follow suit. As Coup attemptor, choose a hand where your cards give you a realistic chance (e.g. Barbu with several Hearts, Siege with long Spades).",
    intermediate: 'As Director, choose the hand that maximizes your chance to collect penalties given the current deal; avoid leading penalty suits first when rules forbid it. When holding the Coup card, attempt a Coup only when your hand supports the chosen objective (e.g. enough Hearts for Barbu, long Spades for Siege). In Waterloo and Siege, consider whether opponents can block you before committing. Track which hands remain in the round so you do not announce an impossible Coup.',
    advanced: 'Use Hidden Coup in Waterloo, Siege, or Guillotine when you can take all penalty cards without revealing intent; bluff early tricks by appearing upset when taking penalty cards so opponents do not counter you. Balance Treasury risk: failed Coup pays the Treasury, which goes to the next successful Coup or the Director at round end. Manage borrowing (200 francs interest per 1000) and repayment from future winnings. In Guillotine, taking all penalty types is hardest but pays 1500 from each; only attempt with very strong hands. In Dominos Coup, the Coup card is not used; sequence planning and forcing the last card on an opponent are key.',
    tips: [
      {
        title: 'Tip',
        description: "Barbu: Dump the King of Hearts on someone else's Ace or 10, or when you cannot follow suit.",
      },
      {
        title: 'Tip',
        description: 'Waterloo: Play Queens on higher cards or discard when not following suit.',
      },
      {
        title: 'Tip',
        description: 'Siege: Get rid of high Spades early; small Spades may be acceptable.',
      },
      {
        title: 'Tip',
        description: 'Touche: Play low on the first trick; save a low card for the last trick.',
      },
      {
        title: 'Tip',
        description: 'Dominos: Hold cards that run in sequence; avoid having only highest or lowest values early.',
      },
